===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make something [[fluffy]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2013|author=Tony Beck|title=The Quest of Millie Blackbeard|page=69|passage=Graham '''fluffled''' his fur and gave Baggly a weak smile. “We did need to be change'n ourselves aunty Baggly. We did be make'n ourselves to be smaller and more cuteful, and of course, we did be need'n to change our throats so that we could be learn'n to be speak'n with our mouths. {{...}}”}}
#: ''The cat '''fluffed''' its tail.''
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To become fluffy, [[puff up]].
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To move lightly like fluff.
#* {{quote-book|en|1872|{{w|Oliver Wendell Holmes Sr.}}|The Poet at the Breakfast-Table|passage=She gave the music-stool a twirl or two and '''fluffed''' down on to it like a whirl of soap-suds in a hand-basin.}}
# {{lb|en|informal|transitive|intransitive|of an actor or announcer}} To make a mistake in one's lines.
#: {{synonyms|en|flub}}
# {{lb|en|informal|transitive}} To do incorrectly, for example [[mishit]], [[miskick]], [[miscue]] etc.
#: {{synonyms|en|flub}}
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=June 19, 2012
|author=Phil McNulty
|title=England 1-0 Ukraine
|work=BBC Sport
|url=http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/0/football/18181971
|page=
|passage=Either side of Rooney's '''fluffed''' chance, it was a tale of Ukrainian domination as they attacked England down both flanks and showed the greater fluidity of the teams.}}
